# fastverk/cred-helper — build config. All deps are public (BCR + crates.io),
# so no credential helper / registry auth is needed to build this repo.

common --registry=https://bcr.bazel.build/

# crate_universe isolated usage (matches the fastverk meta repo).
common --experimental_isolated_extension_usages

# ─── hermetic_cc_toolchain (zig) sandbox mounts + linux link flags ───
# Zig writes its cache under /tmp (linux) / /var/tmp (macos); let the sandbox
# reach it. On linux, disable section GC so lld keeps protobuf/upb's linkarr
# section (the __start_/__stop_ encapsulation symbols), matching the fastverk
# meta repo's hard-won cross-compile config.
common --enable_platform_specific_config
build:macos --sandbox_add_mount_pair=/var/tmp
build:linux --sandbox_add_mount_pair=/tmp
build:linux --host_linkopt=-Wl,--no-gc-sections
build:linux --linkopt=-Wl,--no-gc-sections

# ─── No remote cache. This is deliberate; do not re-add one ─────────
# There used to be a `build:remote` block pointing --remote_cache/--bes_backend
# at grpcs://remote.buildbuddy.io, authenticated by BUILDBUDDY_API_KEY. It is
# gone, for two measured reasons.
#
# ⭐ 1. It never served a cache hit. Bazel's `N processes:` line names every
#    strategy that produced a result, and `remote cache hit` appears in ZERO
#    release runs. Two runs, the two interesting cases:
#      * disk cache WARM  (run 30153785337) — 87s, "780 disk cache hit,
#        784 internal, 1 darwin-sandbox". Every hit came from the GitHub
#        Actions disk cache that setup-bazel restores. Remote: nothing.
#      * disk cache COLD  (run 30126526020, "Cache not found for keys") —
#        361s, "784 internal, 781 darwin-sandbox". 781 actions executed
#        locally. That is precisely the case a remote cache exists to save,
#        and it saved none of it.
#    A remote cache that has never answered is not a speed/safety trade-off,
#    it is an unused credential. `bazel-contrib/setup-bazel`'s `disk-cache:
#    true` is doing the whole job (87s vs 361s), and it needs no secret.
#
# ⛔ 2. The auth mechanism leaks. `--remote_header=x-buildbuddy-api-key=$KEY`
#    puts the key in bazel's ARGV, where it is readable via `ps aux` by any
#    other process on the runner for the life of the build. GitHub's secret
#    masking covers log text; it does not cover a process command line. A
#    live BuildBuddy key leaked from this estate on 2026-08-04 (via a BEP
#    fixture), and this repo was one of the places the key was still in use.
#
# ⚠ If a remote cache is ever wanted here, point it at roma (the estate's
#   REAPI cache) via the credential helper this repo BUILDS — never a bare
#   `--remote_header` with a secret in it. But measure first: the numbers
#   above say a 3-target repo does not need one.

test --test_output=errors
test --test_summary=terse
